# Migration SQL is checksummed and recorded in the schema ledger, and its
# `$function$ ... $function$` bodies are stored in the database verbatim. A
# CRLF checkout therefore changes both the checksum and the stored function
# text for a commit that has not changed at all — which is exactly what
# happened on a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true.
#
# Pinning these files to LF in the working tree makes the bytes on disk the
# same on every machine. The code no longer depends on it — see
# server/lib/canonicalText.js — but the two together mean neither a fresh
# checkout nor a fresh clone can reintroduce the difference.
*.sql text eol=lf
